s/api.py","summary":"pre_save sets the token through the helper. resend_invitation rotates the token before it sends the email. InvitationViewSet.get_queryset only returns invitations that have not expired."},{"path":"taiga/projects/validators.py","summary":"token and token_expires_at are now read-only in MembershipValidator."},{"path":"taiga/export_import/services/store.py","summary":"Imported memberships get the token and expiration date from the helper. Removed the unused uuid import."},{"path":"taiga/projects/management/commands/sample_data.py","summary":"Sample invitations use the helper, so they have a valid expiration date."},{"path":"tests/factories.py","summary":"MembershipFactory and InvitationFactory set token_expires_at to now + 7 days."},{"path":"tests/integration/test_memberships.py","summary":"Tests for: the helper, create and bulk create setting the expiration date (client values are ignored), resend changing the token (old link 404, new link 200), and GET by token for a valid, an expired and an old token."},{"path":"tests/integration/test_auth.py","summary":"Tests that login and private register reject expired and old invitation tokens with 404 and accept nothing. Added a test that private register works with a valid invitation."},{"path":"tests/integration/test_importer_api.py","summary":"Test that an imported invitation gets a token valid for one week and that an expiration date in the import data is ignored."},{"path":"docs/harness/log.md","summary":"Added a 2026-11-02 entry for this change."}],"acceptance":[{"criterion":"Expired and legacy invitation tokens are rejected everywhere (GET invitation, login, register)","met":true,"evidence":"test_get_invitation_by_expired_or_legacy_token_returns_404, test_get_auth_token_with_expired_or_legacy_invitation_is_rejected and test_private_register_with_expired_or_legacy_invitation_is_rejected pass, each for both the expired case and the no-date case."},{"criterion":"Resending gives a new valid token and the old one stops working","met":true,"evidence":"test_api_resend_invitation_rotates_token: the token changes, the expiration date is now + 7 days, the email contains the new token, the old token returns 404 and the new one returns 200."},{"criterion":"Every issuer sets the token and its expiration date through one shared helper","met":true,"evidence":"The API create, bulk create, import and sample_data all use generate_invitation_token or set_invitation_token. Covered by test_api_create_invitation_sets_token_expiration, test_api_create_bulk_invitations_sets_token_expiration and test_valid_project_import_sets_invitation_token_expiration."},{"criterion":"Factories create invitations that expire one week from now","met":true,"evidence":"tests/factories.py: token_expires_at = LazyFunction(now + 7 days) on MembershipFactory and InvitationFactory."},{"criterion":"The change is covered by tests","met":true,"evidence":"pytest on test_memberships.py, test_auth.py and test_importer_api.py: 155 passed. I could not confirm that the new tests fail on the old code, because the revert-and-rerun command was blocked."},{"criterion":"The existing test suite still passes","met":false,"evidence":"make check-fast passes (238) and the 3 related files pass (155). The full make test run (1761 tests, log in /tmp/taiga-full-test.log) had not finished when I had to answer. No failures were seen so far."}],"human_needed":[{"question":"When this is deployed, all pending invitations sent before it stop working because they have no expiration date. Is this acceptable, or should a data migration give them a grace period (for example now + 7 days)?","why":"The task says to treat old tokens as expired. Without a migration, admins must resend every pending invitation after the deploy."},{"question":"Is it acceptable that token and token_expires_at can no longer be set through the memberships API?","why":"Before this change, a client could send its own token. That would bypass the one-week limit, so I made both fields read-only. This changes the API for any client that relied on it."}],"harness_used":["AGENTS.md/CLAUDE.md: commands (make check-fast, make test, make db-up), single-file pytest commands, the --create-db advice, conventions and the instruction to add a log entry","docs/harness/log.md: format for the new entry","make db-up and the compose PostgreSQL for the integration tests","make check-fast as the fast gate"],"harness_gaps":[{"file":null,"problem":"Running the full suite takes about 15 minutes, and there is no faster documented way to run only the tests that touch memberships, invitations and auth. I had to pick the test files by hand."},{"file":"AGENTS.md","problem":"flake8 on a changed file shows many old violations mixed with new ones. The harness has no way to lint only the changed lines (for example flake8 on the diff), so it is hard to prove that new code is clean."},{"file":null,"problem":"Invitation and token lifetimes are not documented. The transfer token period is hard-coded in taiga/projects/services/transfer.py, and the password recovery period is a setting. Nothing in docs/product.md or docs/architecture.md describes how long tokens are valid."}]},"ttft_ms":1722,"type":"result","duration_ms":279850,"uuid":"cf39cbe8-244b-4329-a1d9-974466fca73f","ttft_stream_ms":1595,"time_to_request_ms":163,"first_content_frame_ms":1595,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":94,"outputTokens":18389,"cacheReadInputTokens":2796354,"cacheCreationInputTokens":67915,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.4707468,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":2588,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":67915,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}}}

