{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EktVPd5ouokWrwjzpmYrLv","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Harness log\n2\t\n3\tOne entry per significant change: date, what changed, what was learned, what is left.\n4\t\n5\t## Notes from the harness build\n6\t\n7\t- **Lint is limited in the gates.** `flake8 .` with the `setup.cfg` rules reports 1309 violations in existing code (top codes: F401 163, E501 118, E402 118, E231 84, E252 78). CI never ran flake8 before. The gates run `flake8 --select=E9,F63,F7 .` (syntax errors and invalid comparisons), which passes. `make lint-full` runs the full rules. No rule was added to the flake8 configuration.\n8\t- **Undefined names (F821) in product code, left for a human.** `taiga/projects/userstories/filters.py:45-47` uses `logger` and `exc` without importing them: `UserStoryStatusesFilter` raises `NameError` instead of `BadRequest` for a non-integer `project` parameter. On `GET /api/v1/userstories` the bug is masked because `CanViewUsFilterBackend` runs first and already returns 400, so it is latent. `taiga/base/fields.py:111-133` uses `ValidationError` and `NestedValidationError` without importing them. `taiga/projects/attachments/services.py:95` uses string type hints for models that are not imported (no runtime effect). `taiga/events/middleware.py` has three unused `global _local` statements (F824).\n9\t- **Unit tests are the fast gate.** `make check-fast` runs `tests/unit` (238 tests, about 30 s with a warm test database). Integration tests run only in `make check`.\n10\t- **The full gate needs a fresh test database.** A first `make check` with `--reuse-db` had 51 failures in `tests/integration/test_hooks_*`: transactional tests had flushed the reused database, so the system users created by a data migration were missing. `make check` and `make test` now use `--create-db`, like CI. The fast gate keeps `--reuse-db` (unit tests do not need that data).\n11\t- **The full suite is slow.** `make check` runs all 1751 collected tests with coverage in about 15 minutes on a laptop. Most time is in fixture setup: `tests/factories.py` hashes a password for each user with PBKDF2 (`PASSWORD_HASHERS` in `settings/common.py`). A faster hasher in `tests/config.py` would speed it up, but it changes test settings and needs a team decision.\n12\t- **Tests need PostgreSQL.** The gates start it with `docker compose up -d --wait postgres` (`make db-up`) unless `CI` is set. The compose service runs with `fsync=off`; without it, the first test run took about 100 s for the unit tests alone on Docker for Mac.\n13\t- **Git hook.** The sandbox did not allow writing `.pre-commit-config.yaml`, so the pre-push hook is `.githooks/pre-push`, installed with `git config core.hooksPath .githooks` by `make setup`.\n14\t- **CI.** `.github/workflows/tests-and-coverall.yml` now runs `npx -y uw-harness verify` (setup, check-fast, check) instead of calling pytest directly. `make check` keeps the same coverage command, so the Coveralls step still finds `.coverage`. The unit tests run twice in CI (fast gate, then full gate). On 2026-11-01 `npx -y uw-harness` returned 404 from the npm registry: the CI step fails until the package is published (or the step is changed to call `make check` directly).\n15\t- **Dev dependency added.** `flake8` in `requirements-devel.in`; `requirements-devel.txt` regenerated with `pip-compile` without `--upgrade` (only additions: flake8, mccabe, pycodestyle, pyflakes).\n16\t- **Secret in tracked code, not changed.** `settings/common.py:249` holds a hard-coded `SECRET_KEY`. See the TODO in `AGENTS.md` and the `blocked` list of the harness build.\n17\t\n18\t## 2026-11-01: fast gate output shows the test run\n19\t\n20\t- **What changed.** `make test-unit` (used by `make check-fast`) ran `pytest tests/unit --reuse-db -q`. The `-q` flag hides the pytest header (\"test session starts\", \"collected N items\") and the file names, so the harness verifier reported that the fast gate ran no tests, although 238 tests passed. The target now runs `pytest tests/unit --reuse-db -rA --tb=short`: the output shows the header, one line per test file, one `PASSED <test id>` line per test and the final summary (`238 passed`). No test or check was removed.\n21\t- **What we learned.** A local output filter (rtk) can also truncate `make` output in an agent session; use `rtk proxy make check-fast` to see the real output.\n22\t- **What is left.** Nothing for this gate.\n23\t\n24\t## 2026-11-01: harness built by uw-harness 0.3.0 with claude"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9d474e49-5d0c-494f-840a-4c52349766d2","uuid":"c957c498-32e7-4574-9a50-bae8c02d191e","timestamp":"2026-11-01T23:23:19.905Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/victor/Repos/unwritten/uw-harness-cases/taiga/bench/trees/taiga-1-harness/docs/harness/log.md","content":"# Harness log\n\nOne entry per significant change: date, what changed, what was learned, what is left.\n\n## Notes from the harness build\n\n- **Lint is limited in the gates.** `flake8 .` with the `setup.cfg` rules reports 1309 violations in existing code (top codes: F401 163, E501 118, E402 118, E231 84, E252 78). CI never ran flake8 before. The gates run `flake8 --select=E9,F63,F7 .` (syntax errors and invalid comparisons), which passes. `make lint-full` runs the full rules. No rule was added to the flake8 configuration.\n- **Undefined names (F821) in product code, left for a human.** `taiga/projects/userstories/filters.py:45-47` uses `logger` and `exc` without importing them: `UserStoryStatusesFilter` raises `NameError` instead of `BadRequest` for a non-integer `project` parameter. On `GET /api/v1/userstories` the bug is masked because `CanViewUsFilterBackend` runs first and already returns 400, so it is latent. `taiga/base/fields.py:111-133` uses `ValidationError` and `NestedValidationError` without importing them. `taiga/projects/attachments/services.py:95` uses string type hints for models that are not imported (no runtime effect). `taiga/events/middleware.py` has three unused `global _local` statements (F824).\n- **Unit tests are the fast gate.** `make check-fast` runs `tests/unit` (238 tests, about 30 s with a warm test database). Integration tests run only in `make check`.\n- **The full gate needs a fresh test database.** A first `make check` with `--reuse-db` had 51 failures in `tests/integration/test_hooks_*`: transactional tests had flushed the reused database, so the system users created by a data migration were missing. `make check` and `make test` now use `--create-db`, like CI. The fast gate keeps `--reuse-db` (unit tests do not need that data).\n- **The full suite is slow.** `make check` runs all 1751 collected tests with coverage in about 15 minutes on a laptop. Most time is in fixture setup: `tests/factories.py` hashes a password for each user with PBKDF2 (`PASSWORD_HASHERS` in `settings/common.py`). A faster hasher in `tests/config.py` would speed it up, but it changes test settings and needs a team decision.\n- **Tests need PostgreSQL.** The gates start it with `docker compose up -d --wait postgres` (`make db-up`) unless `CI` is set. The compose service runs with `fsync=off`; without it, the first test run took about 100 s for the unit tests alone on Docker for Mac.\n- **Git hook.** The sandbox did not allow writing `.pre-commit-config.yaml`, so the pre-push hook is `.githooks/pre-push`, installed with `git config core.hooksPath .githooks` by `make setup`.\n- **CI.** `.github/workflows/tests-and-coverall.yml` now runs `npx -y uw-harness verify` (setup, check-fast, check) instead of calling pytest directly. `make check` keeps the same coverage command, so the Coveralls step still finds `.coverage`. The unit tests run twice in CI (fast gate, then full gate). On 2026-11-01 `npx -y uw-harness` returned 404 from the npm registry: the CI step fails until the package is published (or the step is changed to call `make check` directly).\n- **Dev dependency added.** `flake8` in `requirements-devel.in`; `requirements-devel.txt` regenerated with `pip-compile` without `--upgrade` (only additions: flake8, mccabe, pycodestyle, pyflakes).\n- **Secret in tracked code, not changed.** `settings/common.py:249` holds a hard-coded `SECRET_KEY`. See the TODO in `AGENTS.md` and the `blocked` list of the harness build.\n\n## 2026-11-01: fast gate output shows the test run\n\n- **What changed.** `make test-unit` (used by `make check-fast`) ran `pytest tests/unit --reuse-db -q`. The `-q` flag hides the pytest header (\"test session starts\", \"collected N items\") and the file names, so the harness verifier reported that the fast gate ran no tests, although 238 tests passed. The target now runs `pytest tests/unit --reuse-db -rA --tb=short`: the output shows the header, one line per test file, one `PASSED <test id>` line per test and the final summary (`238 passed`). No test or check was removed.\n- **What we learned.** A local output filter (rtk) can also truncate `make` output in an agent session; use `rtk proxy make check-fast` to see the real output.\n- **What is left.** Nothing for this gate.\n\n## 2026-11-01: harness built by uw-harness 0.3.0 with claude","numLines":24,"startLine":1,"totalLines":113}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01EktVPd5ouokWrwjzpmYrLv","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
