{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgd59Q4FJXA6DutUiiHwV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TdCaWaNuLfn2zphURPSUv6","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"status":"done","summary":"Project invitation tokens now expire one week after they are issued, the same period as project transfer tokens. One helper, generate_invitation_token() in taiga/projects/services/invitations.py, returns the token and its expiration date together. Every issuer uses it: membership create, bulk create, project import and sample_data. Only pending invitations with token_expires_at in the future are accepted. Expired tokens and old tokens with no expiration date return 404 on GET /invitations/<token>, on login with invitation_token and on private register, and the invitation is not accepted (on register, no user is created). Resending an invitation gives it a new token and a new expiration date, so the old link stops working. I also made token and token_expires_at read-only in MembershipValidator: before this, an API client could choose its own token or a longer expiration date. Factories now set token_expires_at to now + 7 days. Tests: the related files pass (155) and make check-fast passes (238). The full suite (make test) gave 1752 passed and 9 failed. The 9 failures are logo and avatar upload tests that failed with FileNotFoundError. All 9 passed when I reran them on their own, so they are probably a test-isolation problem with media files, not caused by this change. I did not confirm this in a clean environment. I could not show that the new tests fail on the old code: the command to revert and rerun them was blocked.","changes":[{"path":"taiga/projects/services/invitations.py","summary":"Added INVITATION_TOKEN_LIFETIME (7 days), generate_invitation_token(), set_invitation_token(), rotate_invitation_token() and valid_invitations_queryset(). get_membership_by_token() now rejects expired tokens and tokens with no expiration date."},{"path":"taiga/projects/services/__init__.py","summary":"Exported the new invitation helpers."},{"path":"taiga/projects/services/members.py","summary":"Bulk invitations set the token and token_expires_at through the helper. Removed the unused uuid import."},{"path":"taiga/projects/api.py","summary":"pre_save sets the token through the helper. resend_invitation rotates the token before it sends the email. InvitationViewSet.get_queryset only returns invitations that have not expired."},{"path":"taiga/projects/validators.py","summary":"token and token_expires_at are now read-only in MembershipValidator."},{"path":"taiga/export_import/services/store.py","summary":"Imported memberships get the token and expiration date from the helper. Removed the unused uuid import."},{"path":"taiga/projects/management/commands/sample_data.py","summary":"Sample invitations use the helper, so they have a valid expiration date."},{"path":"tests/factories.py","summary":"MembershipFactory and InvitationFactory set token_expires_at to now + 7 days."},{"path":"tests/integration/test_memberships.py","summary":"Tests for: the helper, create and bulk create setting the expiration date (client values are ignored), resend changing the token (old link 404, new link 200), and GET by token for a valid, an expired and an old token."},{"path":"tests/integration/test_auth.py","summary":"Tests that login and private register reject expired and old invitation tokens with 404 and accept nothing. Added a test that private register works with a valid invitation."},{"path":"tests/integration/test_importer_api.py","summary":"Test that an imported invitation gets a token valid for one week and that an expiration date in the import data is ignored."},{"path":"docs/harness/log.md","summary":"Added a 2026-11-02 entry for this change."}],"acceptance":[{"criterion":"Expired and legacy invitation tokens are rejected everywhere (GET invitation, login, register)","met":true,"evidence":"test_get_invi