itations in real databases have no expiration date and stop working after deploy. Is that acceptable, or should a data migration give them a grace period (for example now + 7 days)?","why":"The task says legacy tokens are treated as expired. Without a migration, admins must resend every pending invitation."}],"harness_used":["AGENTS.md/CLAUDE.md: layout, conventions (taiga.base exceptions, MPL header, gettext, no migration edits), verification steps and the log requirement","Skill .agents/skills/implement-change: test-first flow and the make targets","docs/harness/log.md: entry format","Makefile: lint, test-unit and check targets","tests/factories.py and the existing tests in tests/integration/test_auth.py, test_memberships.py and test_importer_api.py: patterns to copy"],"harness_gaps":[{"file":"tests/config.py","problem":"The test DB name is fixed (test_taiga), and worktrees share the compose PostgreSQL. A parallel session made pytest fail with 'database is being accessed by other users'. I had to create a settings module outside the repo that sets DATABASES['default']['TEST']['NAME']. An env variable for the test DB name would avoid this."},{"file":"Makefile","problem":"The gates hard-code --reuse-db/--create-db on the shared test_taiga database, so make check-fast and make check cannot run safely next to another worktree."},{"file":null,"problem":"The bench environment deleted the worktree while my background full-suite run was still going, so the full-suite result was lost."},{"file":"taiga/projects/services/transfer.py","problem":"The 7-day transfer token lifetime is a literal there, not a setting. INVITATION_TOKEN_LIFETIME repeats the value instead of sharing it."}]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":927,"cache_read_input_tokens":90205,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":927},"output_tokens":8,"